   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the assessor of Mount Pleasant to accept an application\nfor exemption from real property taxes from Spectrum Designs Foundation Ltd.\nfor a certain parcel in the village of Pleasantville in the town of Mount\nPleasant",
    "basePrintNo": "S6599",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6599-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6599\n\nSPONSOR: STEWART-COUSINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the assessor of Mount Pleasant to accept an applica-\ntion for exemption from real property taxes from Spectrum Designs Foun-\ndation Ltd. for a certain parcel in the village of Pleasantville in the\ntown of Mount Pleasant\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to authorize the assessor of the town of\nMount Pleasant to apply a retroactive real property tax exemption for\ncertain property in the town of Mount Pleasant owned by Spectrum Designs\nFoundation Ltd.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the Town of Mount Pleasant, county of Westchester,\nto accept from Spectrum Designs Ltd, an application for exemption from\nreal property taxes.\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSpectrum Designs Foundation Ltd, is a non-profit, custom apparel and\npromotional products organization focused on creating meaningful and\ninclusive employment and vocational training opportunities for neurodi-\nvergent individuals. More than half of its workers are on the autism\nspectrum, and 100 percent of its profits go toward \"the ongoing expan-\nsion and advancement of hiring and retaining an inclusive and integrated\nculture.\" This bill would authorize the assessor of the Town of Mount\nPleasant to accept an application from Spectrum Designs Foundation for\nthe exemption from real property and school taxes pursuant to section\n406-a of the real property law for the 2021-2022 school and real proper-\nty taxes and the 2022-2023 school taxes.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
